cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Entailment Labs benchmarks
message: >-
  If you use these datasets, the harness or any figure from these
  leaderboards, please cite this repository. Cite the version you used:
  a figure is only meaningful with the dataset and harness version that
  produced it.
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  Four benchmark suites for document extraction, voice and chat agents,
  back-office automation and AI operations, built to measure the distance
  between a vendor-deck number and a production number, with every metric
  stated in definitions a business-process outsourcing company can write into
  a statement of work. All data is synthetic. As at this version no suite has
  been run against any system, and every results row reads "not run" with the
  reason.
authors:
  - name: Entailment Labs
    city: Surat
    region: Gujarat
    country: IN
    website: "https://entailmentlabs.com"
    email: hello@entailmentlabs.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/nagu-io/benchmarks"
url: "https://bench.entailmentlabs.com"
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-02"
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - document intelligence
  - information extraction
  - conversational agents
  - containment
  - business process outsourcing
  - evaluation methodology
  - synthetic data
references:
  - type: report
    title: Benchmark charter and methodology
    version: 1.0.0
    authors:
      - name: Entailment Labs
    year: 2026
    notes: >-
      charter/methodology.md in this repository. Defines every metric, its
      numerator, its denominator and its exclusions, the difficulty tiers, the
      neutrality rules, the data ethics, the versioning scheme, the disputes
      process and the limitations. A figure from these suites should be quoted
      with the charter version in force when it was produced.
  - type: report
    title: Benchmark contract clauses
    version: 1.0.0
    authors:
      - name: Entailment Labs
    year: 2026
    notes: >-
      charter/contract-clauses.md in this repository. Clause language for each
      metric, for use in a statement of work or a service schedule. Drafting,
      not legal advice, and not reviewed by a lawyer.
